            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for socks, then the Kannada for a coat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಕಮಲ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಮಲ — kamala — \"a lotus\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಮಲ (kamala) is Sanskrit kamala, \"lotus\", taken over whole as a learned loan, a tatsama (CDIAL 2764). CDIAL, following Mayrhofer, takes the Sanskrit word itself to be a loan from Dravidian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
